==English==

===Etymology===
{{lbor|en|la|interrogātus}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɪnˈtɛrəɡeɪt/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-interrogate.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} to [[question]] or [[quiz]], especially in a [[thorough]] and/or [[aggressive]] manner
#: {{ux|en|The police '''interrogated''' the suspect at some length before they let him go.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|computing}} to [[query]]; to request information from.
#: {{ux|en|to '''interrogate''' a database}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|literary}} to examine critically.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2015|author=Rita Kiki Edozie|author2=Curtis Stokes|title=Malcolm X's Michigan Worldview: An Exemplar for Contemporary Black Studies|publisher=Michigan State University Press
|passage=Griffin's approach allows her to reveal Billie Holiday's resilient strength of character and to '''interrogate''' the racism she endured, which was as tragic as her personal mistakes.}}

